sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Admitted request
    participant B as Competing usage request
    participant H as API handler capacity
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    Note over A,D: Event row: usage_inbox.source = S and usage_inbox.event_id = E
    A->>H: Acquire one buffered-channel slot
    H-->>A: Admitted before body parsing
    A->>A: Validate the usage request
    A->>D: BEGIN, write inbox usage_inbox row batch
    B->>H: Try to acquire a slot without waiting
    alt All slots are occupied
        H-->>B: 503 inbox_unavailable, Retry-After 1
        Note over B,H: No body parsing or database transaction for B
    else A slot is available
        H-->>B: Admit B, normal inbox transaction follows
    end
    A->>D: COMMIT or ROLLBACK the admitted batch
    A->>H: Release its slot when the handler returns
    B->>H: Retry unchanged event identities and content
    H-->>B: Admit if capacity is available
    Note over H,D: Process-local admission semaphore.<br/>Bounds simultaneous usage requests.<br/>Database locks order financial writes.<br/>API processes have separate budgets.
